Una Stubbs: &lsquo;I just think, Oh, I hope I can be good enough&rsquo;
From an interview in the Observer newspaper, viewable over at The Guardian website:
&ldquo;Some people say to me, &lsquo;Oh, did they tell you to play Mrs Hudson like that?&rsquo; Well, no, I just came up with it. I was given the script and I got on with it. I just saw her more like a mother figure to these two boys. There&rsquo;s so much nastiness going on [in the series] that maybe to introduce something a little nicer is a good thing.&rdquo;
Can she see why Benedict Cumberbatch has become a sex symbol? &ldquo;Yes, I can because he&rsquo;s just so unusual. He&rsquo;s joli laid. One minute, you think [she breaks off and does a little moue of distaste], but then the next minute you think, &lsquo;Oh, you&rsquo;re so gorgeous.&rsquo;&rdquo;
Read the entire interview with Una, with a focus on her new play The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time at the National Theatre, here on The Guardian website. 

Una, we heart you.
